- **Physical allowance not pre-drawn** (Muse 4): accepted (§3 step 2, §4.2).
- **Interleaved restrict spuriously refuses diamonds** (Muse 3): accepted —
  closure first, probes exclude the closure (§3).
- **No `keep`; recorded-path history becomes undeletable** (Muse 2):
  accepted — `on delete keep` (§2, §4.3, §6.2).
- **Postcondition too strong** (GPT 6, Muse 12): accepted — scoped to rows
  present when the delete runs (§1, §7).
- **Null-exempt caps break population proofs** (GPT 7, Muse 7): accepted —
  such caps prove no bound; enforcement, activation and device proofs skip the
  null group; an exemption change re-validates (§2.2, §8).
- **Device promise covers retained history and pending writes** (GPT 8),
  **provisional rows and refusal freshness** (Muse 10): accepted (§6.3, §6.4).
- **Set null on a row awaiting deletion** (GPT 9): accepted — deletion
  dominates; every write uses the current image (§3 steps 5–6).
- **Migration misses the read gate; read-through is not a change**
  (GPT 10, Muse 5): accepted (§7, §8, §6.1).
- **Lean campaign would skip every action case** (GPT 11, Muse 11):
