snapback4/crates/snapback4-lang/src/guide/codes.rs:57:    ("E_VIEW_KEY", "row-keyed count views need exactly one conjunctive equality between required references to the same parent, source/member scalar comparisons, and source-only conditions. Declare view unread: count messages by members m where .conversationId = m.conversationId and .ordinal > m.readUpTo; cap members by conversationId. Recount state is engine-owned; read the view instead. Member writers must read the new member and counted group, including public sources. Read counts by member; count-dependent writes or probes may need live-basis recount settlement. Maintenance fields (recountPending, pending and private bookkeeping) cannot decide predicates: use value or member fields; project recountPending as data and check complete. Do not index/rank by value. A source row too large for one recount chunk parks its recount. Any source edit in that member's parent group, including shrinking the oversized row, allows one retry chunk even without a cursor; changing a member field used by the predicate to a different value retries its recount. guide maintains."),
snapback4/crates/snapback4-lang/src/guide/codes.rs:70:    ("N_MAINTAINED_COLUMN_DISCLOSURE", "parent readers learn a count or sum, predicate selection and indexed relative order even without source-row read permission. Restrict the parent audience or use a separate aggregate view if that disclosure is unwanted. guide maintains."),
snapback4/crates/snapback4-lang/src/guide/codes.rs:105:    ("E_TIMELINE_ACTIVATE", "check shares runtime preflight and notes admissible dev launch. dev automatically starts a first-use feed over retained sources: all own events and newest 1,000 live events per current follow, no refill on removal. Deploy needs --allow-feed-adoption; its refusal prints rows to copy and estimated writer lock time at the measured rate. Above 5,000,000 copies it refuses before starting. Writes and syncs wait; devices reacquire. Original event ids are post ids; fresh repost ids and edge epochs do not restore historical delivery. Rename reused owned names. Alternative: query home(c: cursor ?): return activity where .actor = viewer or exists follows[viewer, .actor] last 20 by .at after c. This planned home has no inbox/offline floor and can return complete: false with no next behind unrelated posts. guide feeds."),
snapback4/crates/snapback4-lang/src/guide/codes.rs:106:    ("E_TIMELINE_REDEFINE", "changing a materialized view predicate or sources, or resuming experimental reconstruction, cannot recover edge-admission history or repost identities without their declaration-specific slots; original event ids are post ids. Remove the view and deploy, then add the new definition with a fresh name, or use the feeds card's planned home query over retained sources. Removal preserves sources and resets or retires dependent aggregates. A 0.3 timeline needs its matching engine or a fresh dev store. guide feeds."),
