conservative invalidation. N_LOOKUP_HIDDEN follows the actual read
proof at an actual required point-read gate. A blind mutable update is not
a program read and does not receive N_LOOKUP_HIDDEN merely because its table
write rule admits nonreaders. A required lookup names its actual refusal code;
its note is silent when earlier guards prove that exact row readable. Rebound,
wrong or volatile keys and effectful operands do not establish that witness.
A point update counts as an earlier target
lookup attempt for N_REFERENCE_UNCHECKED, just as a nullable point read does,
including through a known helper only when every successful path performs
that lookup. Silence of that note never proves existence or successful authorization.
These notes change neither authorization nor reference integrity. A reference still validates an id, not existence.

Hidden-lookup candidates are analyzed per required-read occurrence; only surviving
advice is grouped. Named shapes and spreads are opaque effect barriers just
as function helpers are, so they cannot preserve a revoked roster witness.

